  "imagery": "Full-bleed editorial photography is the dominant visual asset: lifestyle, interiors, fashion, and art-direction imagery shot in muted, naturalistic palettes with a slightly desaturated, film-like quality. Photos are presented edge-to-edge (0px radius, no borders, no overlays) and act as the background for overlaid white serif type. The magazine cover and article-grid thumbnails use tight vertical and square crops. There are no illustrations, no abstract graphics, and no iconography beyond a single hamburger glyph; icons are absent because the serif type and the photography carry all semantic weight. Image density is high but never decorative — every photograph serves a story, never an empty card.",
